          <avActivityHighlights>The Avalanche Warning Service currently has only a small amount of information that has been collected in the field. &lt;br/&gt; The fresh snow as well as the wind slabs represent the main danger.</avActivityHighlights>
          <avActivityComment>In particular from starting zones at higher altitudes large natural avalanches, capable of reaching low altitudes, must be expected. Above approximately 2300 m they can be released in the new snow and wind slab layers. &lt;br/&gt; The wind slabs will be deposited on unfavourable layers. They and to be assessed with care and prudence. &lt;br/&gt; Single backcountry tourers can release avalanches. Adjacent to ridgelines and in gullies and bowls and at the base of rock walls the likelihood of avalanches is higher.</avActivityComment>
